  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_COOK",
    "dynamic_line": [
      "Grill's hot.  What'll it be?",
      "Burger, pancakes, chili.  Same as yesterday.  Same as tomorrow.  You get used to it.",
      "Sit anywhere.  The booth by the window's lucky, if you believe in that sort of thing."
    ],
    "responses": [
      { "text": "Let me see the menu.", "effect": "start_trade", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_COOK" },
      { "text": "What's cooking today?", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_MENU" },
      { "text": "How is this place even here?", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_ABOUT" },
      { "text": "Maybe later.", "topic": "TALK_DONE" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_MENU",
    "//": "Says what the cook sells: hot plates that change daily, coffee, almond water; their own kit is not for sale.",
    "dynamic_line": "Five or so plates a day, three or four of each, till they're gone.  Could be burgers, pancakes, waffles, chili, soup, toast, hot dogs, fries.  Coffee always.  Almond water if you're flush.  Menu changes every morning, so if you see something you like, have it.  And no, the pan's not for sale.  If you've got food that's still good, I'll buy it for the kitchen.",
    "responses": [ { "text": "Let me see the menu.", "effect": "start_trade", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_COOK" }, { "text": "Thanks.", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_COOK" } ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_ABOUT",
    "dynamic_line": "Walked in through a fire door that wasn't there the day before.  Grill was warm, fridge was full, nobody home.  Fridge fills itself back up some mornings.  I don't ask.  I cook.  People need somewhere with a door and a light and a hot plate, and this is it.",
    "responses": [ { "text": "Fair enough.", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_COOK" } ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_SERVER",
    "dynamic_line": [
      "Coffee?  It's not good, but it's hot.",
      "Sit down, love, you look like the parking deck chewed you up.",
      "You want to know something, you ask me.  I hear everything at that counter."
    ],
    "responses": [
      { "text": "What's the news?", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_NEWS" },
      { "text": "Who comes in here?", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_REGULARS" },
      { "text": "Just passing through.", "topic": "TALK_DONE" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_NEWS",
    "dynamic_line": [
      "The Exchange put their almond water prices up again.  Bunch of crooks.  Lovely people, but crooks.",
      "One of the Breakroom runners came in last week, ate two plates and slept in the booth.  Said she'd outrun a whole pack.  I believe her.",
      "Fella at the counter swears he found a little room on the level above, dry walls, food in the cupboard, like someone left it for him.  Nobody believed him.  I did.",
      "Lights went out over by the lobbies for an hour.  Someone came in after, white as a sheet, wouldn't say what was grinning at them in the dark.",
      "There's tunnel folk under the garage.  Pipe people.  One of them came up for pancakes, smelled like a boiler, tipped well.",
      "Hounds were at the back door two nights ago.  Cook threw a pan.  They left.  I think they were more scared of him than he was of them."
    ],
    "responses": [
      { "text": "Anything else?", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_NEWS" },
      { "text": "Thanks.", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_SERVER" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BR1_DINER_REGULARS",
    "dynamic_line": "Everyone, sooner or later.  Squatters from the camps, Breakroom people when they can spare the time, traders from the Exchange counting their almond water at the counter.  Folk who've been down here a year and folk who fell in this morning.  Nobody fights in here.  That's the only rule, and the cook enforces it with a frying pan.",
    "responses": [ { "text": "Good rule.", "topic": "TALK_BR1_DINER_SERVER" } ]
  }
]
